---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const stack: [string, string[]][] = [
  ['Systems', ['Linux', 'Bash', 'Ansible', 'Nginx']],
  ['DevOps', ['Docker', 'Kubernetes', 'Helm', 'Git', 'CI/CD']],
  ['Observability', ['Prometheus', 'Alertmanager', 'Grafana', 'Loki', 'ELK Stack', 'OpenTelemetry']],
  ['Data', ['Apache Kafka', 'ClickHouse', 'PostgreSQL', 'MySQL', 'Redis']],
];
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: SITE.name,
  alternateName: SITE.altName,
  url: 'https://bachns.io.vn/about/',
  image: `https://bachns.io.vn${SITE.avatar}`,
  address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Hanoi', addressCountry: 'VN' },
  jobTitle: 'Systems Administrator',
  alumniOf: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'Military Technical Academy', url: 'https://mta.edu.vn/' },
  knowsAbout: ['Linux', 'System Administration', 'Bash', 'Ansible', 'Nginx', 'Docker', 'Kubernetes', 'Helm', 'DevOps', 'CI/CD', 'Observability', 'Monitoring', 'Prometheus', 'Alertmanager', 'Grafana', 'Grafana Loki', 'ELK Stack', 'OpenTelemetry', 'Apache Kafka', 'ClickHouse', 'PostgreSQL', 'MySQL', 'Redis', 'Big Data', 'Data Warehouse', 'Python'],
};
---
<Base title="About" description="About Bach Nguyen, a Linux systems administrator who loves technology, books and coffee, writing from Hanoi, Vietnam.">
  <div class="container about">
    <header class="about-head">
      <div class="about-photo"><img src={SITE.avatar} alt={`${SITE.name} - profile photo`} width="768" height="768" /></div>
      <div>
        <h1>~/about</h1>
        <p class="about-name">{SITE.name} <span>({SITE.altName})</span></p>
        <p class="about-sub">A Linux systems administrator who loves technology, books and coffee.</p>
        <p class="about-loc">📍 {SITE.location}</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="about-lead">
      Hi, I'm <strong>Bach Nguyen</strong>, though some friends call me <em>Mr. Robot</em>.
      I'm the author of this blog, and I'm glad you're curious about the journey behind these pages.
      Grab a coffee if you like, and let me introduce myself.
    </p>

    <p class="about-text">
      I work in system administration: operating Linux systems and observability platforms, and writing some code
      now and then.
    </p>
    <p class="about-text">
      I'm based in Hanoi, Vietnam, and my hometown is in Hung Yen Province, the old Thai Binh Province.
      I studied Information Technology at the <a href="https://mta.edu.vn/">Military Technical Academy</a>,
      and these days I'm fueled by coffee and books, with a game of Chinese chess now and then.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">// tech i work with</h2>
    <p class="about-text">
      My day-to-day is system administration: running Linux systems and keeping them observable.
      I work with DevOps practices, monitoring and Big Data pipelines, and these are the main tools I reach for.
    </p>
    <div class="tech-rows">
      {stack.map(([label, items]) => (
        <div class="tech-row">
          <small>{label}</small>
          <div class="chip-row">{items.map((c) => <span class="tchip">{c}</span>)}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title">// why this blog</h2>
    <p class="about-text">
      This blog is my notebook. Along the road I keep picking up knowledge: a lot about IT systems and Linux, some cryptography,
      some programming, and technology in general. Writing it down helps me remember it,
      and sharing it means someone else might skip a few of the wrong turns I took.
    </p>
    <p class="about-text">
      Here is what you can expect: notes on <a href="/category/sysadmin/">system administration</a>,
      <a href="/category/linux/">Linux</a>, <a href="/category/security/">security</a>,
      <a href="/category/cryptography/">cryptography</a> and <a href="/category/programming/">programming</a>,
      plus some <a href="/category/tech/">tech</a> news and trends. And now and then, a few random things
      that don't fit anywhere else.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">// my journey</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li class="tl">
        <span class="tl-tag">Roots</span>
        <h3>A rice-field childhood</h3>
        <p>I was born and raised in <strong>Hung Yen Province</strong>, in the area that used to be the old
        <strong>Thai Binh Province</strong>, about 100 km south-east of Hanoi. It is farming country.
        Our local specialty is poverty, plus endless rice fields so wide that the storks can fly and fly
        without ever finding a place to land.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="tl">
        <span class="tl-tag">High school</span>
        <h3>The coolest school in town</h3>
        <p>I studied at <strong>Hung Nhan High School</strong>, probably the coolest school in my hometown and the one
        everybody dreams of getting into. It had excellent teachers, and it was just as famous for its
        good-looking students.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="tl">
        <span class="tl-tag">A big decision</span>
        <h3>Uniform and IT</h3>
        <p>In my final year I made a hard decision: I chose the military, and I chose to study
        <strong>Information Technology</strong> at the
        <a href="https://mta.edu.vn/"><strong>Military Technical Academy</strong></a> (MTA).
        It wasn't easy, but I'm still happy and proud that I made that choice.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="tl">
        <span class="tl-tag">Today</span>
        <h3>Still learning, now in public</h3>
        <p>These days I work in system administration in Hanoi, running Linux systems and observability,
        with some programming now and then. I'm still curious, still learning, and writing down
        what I learn here so I can keep it and share it.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="section-title">// beyond the keyboard</h2>
    <p class="about-text">
      Away from the keyboard, you will usually find me with a book or a cup of coffee. I love to read, and books are
      where a lot of my curiosity starts. As for coffee, I can't say exactly when it began, probably while I was
      preparing for the high school entrance exams, when it became my sidekick for staying focused and beating
      sleepiness. Today I drink it every day: morning, afternoon, and sometimes late at night.
    </p>
    <p class="about-text">
      I used to play volleyball, but these days my sport is Xiangqi (Chinese chess). I love how it rewards
      patience and planning ahead, which is not so different from running systems: think a few moves
      ahead, and don't leave anything unguarded.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">// say hello</h2>
    <p class="about-text">
      If you want to talk about technology, or you have feedback on a post, you're always welcome to reach out.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:bachns@outlook.com">Email</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://t.me/bachns">Telegram</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
</Base>
